<article class="env-lemma" id="0DZM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DZM">Lemma <span data-tag="0DZM">93.9.8</span>.</a> In Example <a href="/tag/0DY7" data-tag="0DY7">93.9.1</a> let $X$ be a scheme over $k$ Let $p \in X$ be a point. With $\mathcal{D}\! \mathit{ef}_{\mathcal{O}_{X, p}}$ as in Example <a href="/tag/0DY1" data-tag="0DY1">93.8.1</a> there is a natural functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{D}\! \mathit{ef}_ X \longrightarrow \mathcal{D}\! \mathit{ef}_{\mathcal{O}_{X, p}}  \]
</div>
  <p> of deformation categories. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose an affine open $U = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(P) \subset X$ containing $p$. Then $\mathcal{O}_{X, p}$ is a localization of $P$. We combine the functors from Lemmas <a href="/tag/0DYW" data-tag="0DYW">93.9.6</a>, <a href="/tag/0DYX" data-tag="0DYX">93.9.7</a>, and <a href="/tag/0DYS" data-tag="0DYS">93.8.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>